  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#show-popover\r\n\r\nAfter \"Run [hide all popovers until](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/popover.html#hide-all-popovers-until) given ancestor, false, and true.\"\r\nThe element could move to other document.  For instance, https://jsbin.com/yizayoyemu/edit?html,js,output\r\n\r\n```\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<div id='popover0' popover=\"auto\">\r\n    <p>this is popover0</p>\r\n    <div id='popover1' style=\"top:10px;\" popover=\"auto\"><p>This is popver1</p></div>\r\n    <div id='popover2' popover=\"auto\"><p>This is a popver2</p></div>\r\n</div>\r\n<iframe id=\"myFrame\" srcdoc=\"<p>iframe</p>\"></iframe>\r\n\r\n<script>\r\nvar popover2 = document.getElementById('popover2');\r\npopover1.addEventListener('beforetoggle', (e) => {\r\n    if(e.newState == \"closed\") {\r\n        popover2.remove();\r\n        myFrame.contentWindow.document.body.appendChild(popover2);\r\n    }\r\n});\r\n\r\npopover0.showPopover();\r\nsetTimeout(() => {\r\n    popover1.showPopover();\r\n    setTimeout(() => {\r\n        popover2.showPopover();\r\n    }, 1000);\r\n}, 1000);\r\n</script>\r\n```\r\n\r\n`popover2` moves to iframe when call `showPopover`.\r\nShould we continue or return from here? Any ideas? @emilio @nt1m @jakearchibald \r\n",
